{title: Abide with Me}
{artist: Henry F. Lyte}
{key: D}
{tempo: 60}
{time: 4/4}
{meta: tune EVENTIDE - William H. Monk (1861)}
{meta: public_domain Text 1847, tune 1861: both published before 1931 (US public domain); all authors, translators and composers died over 70 years ago. Chords and section layout: original simple arrangement by Tabernacle Tools. Original verses only, no modern additions.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
A[D]bide with [A]me; [D]fast falls the [G]even[D]tide;
The [D]darkness [Bm]deepens; [E]Lord, with me a[A]bide.
When [D]other [A]helpers [D]fail and [G]comforts [D]flee,
[G]Help of the [D]helpless, [A]O a[A7]bide with [D]me.
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Swift [D]to its [A]close [D]ebbs out life's [G]little [D]day;
Earth's [D]joys grow [Bm]dim; its [E]glories pass a[A]way;
Change [D]and de[A]cay in [D]all a[G]round I [D]see;
[G]O Thou who [D]changest [A]not, a[A7]bide with [D]me.
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
I [D]fear no [A]foe, with [D]Thee at [G]hand to [D]bless;
Ills [D]have no [Bm]weight, and [E]tears no bitter[A]ness.
Where [D]is death's [A]sting? Where, [D]grave, thy [G]victo[D]ry?
I [G]triumph [D]still, if [A]Thou a[A7]bide with [D]me.
{end_of_verse}
